<title>USA: USDA buys 36,000 lbs frozen hams for programs.</title>
<headline>USDA buys 36,000 lbs frozen hams for programs.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agricultural Marketing Service of the U.S. Agriculture Department said it bought 36,000 lbs of frozen smoked fully cooked boneless hams for use in the National School Lunch Program and other programs.</p>
<p>AMS said it bought the hams for $1.9450 per lb from Clougherty Packing Co. Shipments are scheduled for Nov 13 to 26.</p>
<p>It said cumulative purchases since the frozen pork buying program was announced Aug 19 are as follows:</p>
<p> Pork Product		     Cumulative</p>
<p>				Lbs		   Dollars</p>
<p>Coarse Ground	 2,217,600	     2,387,000</p>
<p>Fine Ground	   5,029,200	     5,844,000</p>
<p>3 oz Patties	    990,000	     1,316,000</p>
<p>1.5 oz Patties	  594,000		 893,000</p>
<p>Bulk Sausage	    356,400		 433,000</p>
<p>Rib-Shaped		158,400		 291,000</p>
<p>Hams		    4,428,000	     8,476,000</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720</p>
